WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.430
-: The next thing we'll talk about is collaborators.

00:02.430 --> 00:05.160
How do we add collaborators to a repo?

00:05.160 --> 00:06.270
Now that's different, right?

00:06.270 --> 00:08.250
Working with somebody on a GitHub repo is different

00:08.250 --> 00:10.650
from just making a repo public.

00:10.650 --> 00:12.630
When I say working with collaborators,

00:12.630 --> 00:15.930
I mean allowing other users to push changes

00:15.930 --> 00:17.400
to the repository.

00:17.400 --> 00:20.430
When a repo is public, anybody can take, like any

00:20.430 --> 00:22.950
of these public repos, not this one that we made private.

00:22.950 --> 00:26.520
They can take any of these public repos and clone them,

00:26.520 --> 00:28.650
make their own changes and commits,

00:28.650 --> 00:32.730
but they can't push them back up to my copy.

00:32.730 --> 00:35.790
Nobody can just take over a repo

00:35.790 --> 00:37.710
without me granting them permission.

00:37.710 --> 00:39.120
Otherwise, they could delete everything,

00:39.120 --> 00:41.250
and then just push up an empty version.

00:41.250 --> 00:42.240
That's not how it works.

00:42.240 --> 00:45.480
I have to grant people collaboration privileges.

00:45.480 --> 00:46.860
So I'll show you how to do that.

00:46.860 --> 00:48.570
I have two accounts, right?

00:48.570 --> 00:50.490
I already explained that I have Colt

00:50.490 --> 00:52.200
and then I have Stevie,

00:52.200 --> 00:56.550
and why don't I add Stevie to this bookish disco repository

00:56.550 --> 00:58.650
and give him permission to push?

00:58.650 --> 01:01.290
So, I'm logged in, as Colt, the owner.

01:01.290 --> 01:02.730
There's nothing even in here.

01:02.730 --> 01:04.503
If I go into settings,

01:05.460 --> 01:07.920
under settings, we've been here to options.

01:07.920 --> 01:09.090
This is where we change something

01:09.090 --> 01:11.340
from public to private and vice versa.

01:11.340 --> 01:14.160
We also have manage access,

01:14.160 --> 01:18.300
and this is where I can add direct access collaborators.

01:18.300 --> 01:20.040
So here's visibility, right?

01:20.040 --> 01:22.800
Only those with access can even view it in the first place.

01:22.800 --> 01:25.860
Right now, that's just me, just Colt.

01:25.860 --> 01:28.530
But I'm gonna change that, I'm gonna invite Stevie.

01:28.530 --> 01:31.620
So to do that I need to know Stevie's GitHub username

01:31.620 --> 01:33.120
or his email.

01:33.120 --> 01:34.950
Now, I think if I remember,

01:34.950 --> 01:37.590
I just did StevieChicks, like that.

01:37.590 --> 01:39.960
Yep, there he is.

01:39.960 --> 01:41.310
I'm gonna click,

01:41.310 --> 01:44.613
and then I'm gonna add Stevie Chicks to this repository.

01:46.320 --> 01:48.720
Okay, so that's just an invitation.

01:48.720 --> 01:52.890
So Stevie now has to actually go to his email that he signed

01:52.890 --> 01:54.570
up for GitHub with, he'll get a...

01:54.570 --> 01:55.560
or he'll get a message there.

01:55.560 --> 01:58.350
He has to click a link to accept the invite.

01:58.350 --> 02:01.560
So Stevie opens up his email, he clicks the link.

02:01.560 --> 02:04.890
I didn't show you that because it's my email inbox,

02:04.890 --> 02:08.280
but I click the link as Stevie, and this is what we see.

02:08.280 --> 02:10.560
Colt invited you to collaborate,

02:10.560 --> 02:12.030
accept or decline.

02:12.030 --> 02:15.120
So again, you can't just automatically add someone.

02:15.120 --> 02:17.430
It requires permission on both sides.

02:17.430 --> 02:20.640
I have to invite somebody and they have to accept.

02:20.640 --> 02:24.180
And so as Stevie, I will accept, but it does, you know,

02:24.180 --> 02:26.250
it says, here's the information that Colt

02:26.250 --> 02:28.440
and other people will be able to have access to,

02:28.440 --> 02:31.740
your activity, where your request activity is coming from,

02:31.740 --> 02:34.530
basically country of origin, your IP address.

02:34.530 --> 02:37.500
Anyway, I'm gonna hit accept, and now my view changes.

02:37.500 --> 02:40.200
I wasn't able to see this repository just a second ago

02:40.200 --> 02:43.260
because it's private, but now I'm a collaborator.

02:43.260 --> 02:46.980
If I go back to Colt's view, we see now,

02:46.980 --> 02:49.260
if I refresh the page, Stevie Chicks is listed

02:49.260 --> 02:50.520
as a collaborator.

02:50.520 --> 02:53.280
If I want to get rid of him, or multiple collaborators,

02:53.280 --> 02:56.070
I can use check boxes and then delete.

02:56.070 --> 02:58.740
But I am gonna keep him as a collaborator.

02:58.740 --> 03:01.620
And so now, already we can see it's a private repo.

03:01.620 --> 03:04.410
Stevie has access to this repository.

03:04.410 --> 03:05.940
But what I'm gonna demonstrate next is that

03:05.940 --> 03:07.860
Stevie also has push access.

03:07.860 --> 03:10.320
It's not just about viewing the project on GitHub,

03:10.320 --> 03:12.660
although that is new, because it's private,

03:12.660 --> 03:14.340
he's a collaborator, he can view it.

03:14.340 --> 03:17.460
I can also clone and push my changes up.

03:17.460 --> 03:21.210
However, Stevie does not have access to settings, right?

03:21.210 --> 03:22.830
Stevie is not the owner.

03:22.830 --> 03:26.220
Stevie is a collaborator, but the owner is Colt.

03:26.220 --> 03:29.100
I'm the only one who sees settings.

03:29.100 --> 03:32.430
If I go to Stevie's side, that doesn't exist.

03:32.430 --> 03:34.230
So that is an important distinction.

03:34.230 --> 03:36.390
Being a collaborator, it's not like you can

03:36.390 --> 03:37.380
do everything, right?

03:37.380 --> 03:39.120
You can't delete the repository.

03:39.120 --> 03:41.310
I can't invite my own people here.

03:41.310 --> 03:46.080
I can't delete other people or remove their privileges.

03:46.080 --> 03:47.970
With different levels, different tiers,

03:47.970 --> 03:49.800
you definitely can have those features,

03:49.800 --> 03:52.140
like organization and enterprise tiers.

03:52.140 --> 03:55.560
You, on GitHub, you can have multiple owners.

03:55.560 --> 03:57.000
So permissions are different.

03:57.000 --> 03:59.430
So next step, I'll show you what it's like to collaborate

03:59.430 --> 04:00.750
and actually make some commits,

04:00.750 --> 04:03.273
and push them up from two different accounts.
